ntry>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA SHIN</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>SHINOMIYA TADASHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>UMEYAMA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IJI, MASATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SATO, ICHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SERIZAWA, SHIN</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>SHINOMIYA, TADASHI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>UMEYAMA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A flame-retardant polycarbonate resin composition characterized by comprising (A) 100 parts by weight of a polycarbonate resin, (B) 0.01 to 8 parts by weight of a silicone compound in which the main chain has a branched structure and which contains organic substituents comprising aromatic groups, and (C) 0.01 to 2 parts by weight of an alkali metal salt of a specific aromatic sulfonic acid and optionally further containing (D) 0.05 to 5 parts by weight of a fluoropolymer capable of forming fibers. The composition has high flame retardancy while retaining intact impact resistance and moldability. Since the composition contains no halogenated flame retardants comprising a chlorine or boron compound or the like, it has no fear of generating, upon burning, a halogen-containing gas attributable to such a flame retardant. Thus, it has an excellent performance also from the standpoint of environmental protection.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>La présente invention concerne une composition ignifuge de résine de polycarbonate caractérisée en ce qu'elle comprend: (A) 100 parties en poids de résine de polycarbonate, (B) entre 0,01 et 8 parties en poids d'un composé de silicium dans lequel la chaîne principale présente une structure ramifiée, et qui contient des substituants organiques comprenant des groupes aromatiques, et (C) entre 0,01 et 2 parties en poids d'un sel de métal alcalin d'un acide sulfonique aromatique spécifique, cette composition pouvant éventuellement contenir (D) entre 0,05 et 5 % en poids d'un fluoropolymère pouvant former des fibres. En outre, cette composition présente des propriétés hautement ignifuges tout en conservant des propriétés intactes en terme de résistance aux chocs et d'aptitude au moulage. Puisque cette composition ne contient pas d'agents ignifuges halogénés à base de composé de chlore ou de bore ou analogue, elle ne risque pas de produire, après combustion, de gaz d'halogène imputable à ce type d'ignifuges. Ainsi, cette composition présente d'excellentes performances, y compris du point de vue écologique.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>